    {
      "heading": "But flips it",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Although the first speaker was concise, the second rambled for an hour.",
          "write": "Although… concise… rambled"
        },
        {
          "say": "Although signals a contrast. The two speakers were opposites.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Contrast between speakers",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "concise = ?"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 240,
                "y": 120,
                "x2": 320,
                "y2": 120,
                "color": "red"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 120,
                "x2": 240,
                "y2": 120,
                "color": "red"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 330,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "rambled 1 hour"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 220,
                "text": "opposites",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "red",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Rambling is long and wandering. So concise is brief and to the point.",
          "write": "concise = brief, to the point"
        },
        {
          "say": "Loud is the trap. Loud isn't the opposite of rambling.",
          "write": "✗ loud"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Words with more than one meaning",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Short words like draw, flag and weather have surprise meanings.",
          "write": "draw • flag • weather"
        },
        {
          "say": "The team's spirits had flagged. The other side kept scoring.",
          "write": "spirits had flagged"
        },
        {
          "say": "You know flag as a banner. Does that fit? No.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Meanings of flagged",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "change": "remove",
                "label": "marked with a flag"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "change": "remove",
                "label": "signalled for help"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 160,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "change": "highlight",
                "label": "grown weaker"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 160,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "change": "remove",
                "label": "become angry"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Losing and going quiet means losing energy. Flagged means grown weaker.",
          "write": "flagged = grown weaker"
        },
        {
          "say": "Figures of speech too. The jewel of the street means most admired.",
          "write": "jewel = most admired"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Back-ups and traps",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Word parts help. Il means not, so illegible means can't be read.",
          "write": "il + legible = not readable",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Illegible from parts",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "il = not"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 220,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 280,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "legible"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 230,
                "text": "illegible = can't be read",
                "size": 26,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "But illegible is not illegal. Read the letters carefully.",
          "write": "illegible ≠ illegal"
        },
        {
          "say": "Think about feeling. Frugal is positive. Stingy is negative.",
          "write": "frugal (+)   stingy (−)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Beware options that are true in the story but aren't the meaning."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Cover, predict, swap.",
          "write": "Cover, predict, swap"
        },
        {
          "say": "Five clues: definition, synonym, contrast, example, general sense.",
          "write": "DSCEG"
        },
        {
          "say": "After but, although or unlike, look for an opposite.",
          "write": "but flips it"
        },
        {
          "say": "Small word, big trap. Check which meaning fits this sentence.",
          "write": "small word, big trap"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
